{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327064-let-s-make-antagonists-of-fantasy-series-into-true-fae","id":327064,"title":"Let's make antagonists of fantasy series into True Fae!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-01T08:57:18-08:00","id":327064,"title":"Let's make antagonists of fantasy series into True Fae!","content":"As the title goes. A fun little thought experiment that came from me writing the details for an original fae and all his Titles, which then led to a discussion with a friend over antagonists and villains of well known series who could easily be reimagined into True Fae. I'm sure we weren't the only ones to have those thoughts, so come on in and share what you thought up if you want!<br /> <br /> Two examples me and my friend discussed more than once: <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>The Lord Of Burning Wastes, Sargeras</i> (Warcraft franchise)</span><br /> <br /> <i>Name:</i> Sargeras<br /> <i>Actor:</i> The Deceiver (Kil'Jaeden)<br /> <i>Actor:</i> The Defiler (Archimonde)<br /> <i>Actor:</i> The Destructor (Mannoroth)<br /> <i>Actor:</i> The Darkener (Tichondrius)<br /> <i>Wisps:</i> The Burning Legion (The myriad demons of the Burning Legion)<br /> <i>Realm:</i> The Home Of Warlocks (Argus, the homeworld of the Eredar)<br /> <i>Prop:</i> The Dark Seether (Gorribal, Sargeras's sword) <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>The Dark Lord Of Middle-Earth, Sauron</i></span> (Lord Of The Rings)<br /> <br /> <i>Name:</i> Sauron<br /> <i>Actor:</i> The Lord Of Gifts (as he appeared to the elves in the form of Annatar, Lord Of Gifts)<br /> <i>Actor: </i>The Necromancer (his physical body during the events of The Hobbit and the Lord Of The Rings trilogy)<br /> <i>Realm: </i>The Land Of Shadows (Mordor, of course)<br /> <i>Wisps: </i>The Dark Wraiths (The Nazgul)<br /> <i>Prop: </i>The One To Rule Them All (the One Ring)<br /> <br /> <br /> Sargeras was mostly brainspew with aforementioned friend, but I did start writing the sheets for Sauron, which I won't share at the time because of their current incompleteness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T04:56:01-07:00","id":631023,"title":"","content":"YHWH, God the creator <br /> Actor- The son (Jesus)<br /> Actor- The deceiver (Lucifer)<br /> Realm- Heaven<br /> Realm- Hell <br /> Wisps- The choir of angels <br /> Wisps- The fallen<br /> Prop- Holy grail (cup of life)<br /> <br /> Pretending to his captives that he is at war with another powerful being (satan) he uses the idea of free will in his realms to create legends off of changeling warfare that believe they are fighting for one side or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3837-slimjimjohnson","name":"Slimjimjohnson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T06:10:31-07:00","id":631094,"title":"","content":"<i>The Lady of Dreaming Mists</i><br /> <br /> Name Actor: The Deathly Savior (Izanami)<br /> <br /> Actor: The Fog of the Heavens (Ameno-sagiri)<br /> <br /> Exiled Actor: Blur of Tears (Kusumi-no-Okami/Marie)<br /> <br /> Prop: The Fools' Mantles (Persona-granting power)<br /> <br /> Prop: Shadow's Bleak Prophecy (Midnight Channel)<br /> <br /> Realm: Nightmare's Prison (Yomotosu Hirasaka)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T07:14:04-07:00","id":631149,"title":"","content":"True Fae: The Mother of Night (Nyx from Persona 3)<br /> Actor: The Graceful Angel of Deathly Curtains (Nyx Avatar)<br /> Actor: The Boy in Stripes (Pharos)<br /> Wisps: The Twelve Shards (the Arcana-derived boss Shadows)<br /> Realm: The Tower Without an Hour (Tartarus and the Dark Hour)<br /> Realm: The Womb that Is the Grave (the inside of the moon)<br /> Prop: Hallowed Feathers of Twilight (the Nyx Feathers used to craft Evokers and tech that work in the Dark Hour- forgot their in-game name)<br /> <br /> Charlatan: The Boy with Ominous Allure (Ryoji) - exiled form of the Boy in Stripes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5789-acanthus","name":"acanthus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T07:21:13-07:00","id":631153,"title":"","content":"True Fae: Flight From Death (Voldemort from the Harry Potter series)<br /> Actor: The Liche-Sorcerer (Voldemort himself)<br /> Actor: The Corpse-Eating Coil (Nagini)<br /> Prop: Seducement of Murder (Tom Riddle's Diary)<br /> Prop: Horcruxes (the other Horcruxes of relatively little significance)<br /> Wisp: The Death-Eaters (yup)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5789-acanthus","name":"acanthus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T09:31:33-07:00","id":631266,"title":"","content":"I love Voldemort! That's awesome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3837-slimjimjohnson","name":"Slimjimjohnson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T23:55:57-07:00","id":632032,"title":"","content":"Alright, time to get really nerdy:<br /> <br /> <i>Name: </i>The Eternal Adversary (Naar, the god of darkness from Joe Dever's <i>Lone Wolf</i> books)<br /> <br /> <i>Actor:</i> The Mad King Ascendant (The Darklords of Helgedad, timeless beings racked by endless pain and hatred for all that lives. Though said to number twenty in all, they never seem to act together, and outside of the current Archlord, they're generally little more than rumors)<br /> <br /> <i>Prop:</i> Hate Given Form (The Doomstones of Agarash the Damned, mystic weapons inimical to all life, even that of their wielder)<br /> <br /> <i>Realm:</i> The Suffocating Night (the Darklands, a barren realm where the very earth and air are toxic, ruled from Helgedad, a vast city-fortress in the center of a lake of mystic fire)<br /> <br /> <i>Wisps:</i> The Devouring Dark (The Zlanbeasts, leathery-winged, saw-beaked flying mounts for the Darklords and their officers, and the Kraan, their smaller cousins who descend from the skies in great black clouds of death)<br /> <br /> <i>Wisps:</i> Driver of the Damned (The Legions of the Darklords, consisting mainly of Giaks, the grey-skinned, yellow-eyed inhabitants of the Darklands, and the Drakkarim, human soldiers from lands conquered by the Darklords)<br /> <br /> <i>Wisps:</i> The Pernicious Gift (The Nadziranim, masters of evil sorcery known for tempting the morally weak with forbidden teachings and artifacts of terrible power)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 08-19-2015, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T14:45:34-07:00","id":642099,"title":"","content":"The AntiEmissary<br /> <br /> Actor: Gul Dukat<br /> Actor: Kia Wynn<br /> Actor: The Great Link (female Changeling)<br /> Realm: The Dominion<br /> Wisps: The Pahwraiths","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T19:59:40-07:00","id":644886,"title":"","content":"Revolutionary Girl Utena is an anime that plays with fairy-tales, and the roles that they force people into.<br /> <br /> Also there's a movie that ends with something resembling an escape from Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Name Actor: The Fallen Prince (Akio Ohtori, who dragged people into his world and manipulated them into playing the roles he needed to reenact Dios' story.)<br /> Actor: The Rose Bride (Anthy Himemiya, Akio's abused sister, forced to play the role of a &quot;Wicked Witch&quot; in Akio's story.)<br /> <b>Former Actor</b>: The Ideal Prince (Dios, who Akio <i>was</i> until he was confronted with both an angry mob and the realization that as the &quot;Prince Charming&quot; character, couldn't save his own sister)<br /> Prop: Traveler on the Endless Road (Akio's Car, which he uses to seduce people when he's not cruising around the dark outer edges of his world.)<br /> Prop: The Illusory Architecture (The planetarium projector, which projects among other things, A floating castle, a confessional-elevator, and <i>working cars</i>.)<br /> Prop: The Rose Seals (The rose rings, which force their wearers into ritual fencing duels over custody of The Rose Bride)<br /> Realm: The Prince's Coffin (Ohtori Acadamy, the world Akio created when he &quot;died&quot; as Dios, containing a high-school, a tower, and an endless dark road)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T22:18:18-07:00","id":644923,"title":"","content":"The Gentleman With Thistledown Hair, from Suzanna Clarke's &quot;Jonathan Strange &amp; Mr. Norrell&quot;, recently adapted into a TV series by the BBC. He is actually one of the main inspirations for the True Fae, and the book is cited in the recommendations section of the 1ed core book.<br /> <br /> True Name: Not mentioned in the book or TV series, as far as I know. Probably something very pretentious and rather convoluted, but still comprehensible.<br /> <br /> Actor: The Aristocratic Whispers. The entity we think of as the Gentleman.<br /> <br /> Realm: Lost Hope. A very opulent and impressive mansion with Gothic and Victorian aesthetics, but with a very ghostly weather surrounding and filling it. It's illusory residents and True Fae visitors are profoundly elitist in garment and demeanor. However, they have numerous small marks of decadence and ugliness, such as an odor of roses with a hint of rotting corpses, old bloodstains and animal-like visage. They often try to hide these imperfections with make-up, masks and other accessories, but only make themselves look even more fake and arrogant. Their imitations of noble pastimes and mannerisms are pale at best, and abhorrent at worst.<br /> <br /> 1ed Seeming And Kith Blessings: Fairest + Lyrical Voice (True Fae), Perfect Protocol (Chatelaine) and Shadow Beauty (Illes).<br /> <br /> 1ed Contracts: Vainglory, Separation, Smoke, Mirror, Omen, Darkness, Control The Elements, Communion With The Elements.<br /> <br /> 1ed Goblin Contracts: Fool's Gold, Mirror Mirror, Delayed Harm, Diviner's Madness, Fair Entrance.<br /> <br /> Frailties: Must always act in an aristocratic manner, even when in the grip of strong emotions (Major Taboo), when he makes his presence known, must make at least one scornful remark about the features and choices of others that he deems improper or undesirable (Minor Taboo), must avoid direct physical confrontation, be it through guile, magic or stealthy kills (Minor Taboo).<br /> <br /> If you want to make him more capable of defending himself when cornered, you could give him dots in the Stone Contract, the Lethal Mien and Charmed Life Merits, and make his characteristic garments a Hedgespun Raiment with Armor.<br /> <br /> Also, he has the Manifest Mien Flaw, which makes his Lyrical Voice audible through the Mask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-03-2015, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T23:31:51-07:00","id":645060,"title":"","content":"<b>GottaGoFeast</b>, with your's permission, I would add this analysis to out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/620130-jonathan-strange-mr-norrell-as-awakening-game\">'Johnathan Strange &amp; Mr Norrell' as Mage</a> game topic. Or you could post it there, yourself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, as to Name of Gentlemen - in episode 5 or 6 he was called as Blue Corbel ( or something like this ), Man in Blue. I need to look for the scene, but I remember, as watched it only week ago. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-30-2015, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T11:54:14-07:00","id":650373,"title":"","content":"Too busy to try stating them up right now, but the Deadric Princes from The Elder Scrolls games are all fine examples of Gentry, espcially Sheogorath, The Mad God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T21:03:42-07:00","id":675994,"title":"","content":"<i>Freddy Fazbear</i> from <i>Five Nights at freddy's</i> (not that I really need to mention that, let's be honest)<br /> <br /> Realm: Freddy Fazbear's Pizza<br /> Actors: Freddy (all versions), Bonnie (all versions), Chica (all versions), Foxy (all versions), Balloon Boy, Marionette, Purple Guy<br /> Props: Cameras &amp; Screen, Electronic Doors, Freddy Mask, Systems, Flashlight<br /> Wisps: Phone Guy<br /> <br /> A True Fae that pits its slaves to work as &quot;security guards&quot; and constantly kills them again and again. So yeah, think about that next time you play FNAF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T22:13:25-07:00","id":680676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327064-let-s-make-antagonists-of-fantasy-series-into-true-fae?p=675994#post675994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Freddy Fazbear</i> from <i>Five Nights at freddy's</i> (not that I really need to mention that, let's be honest)<br /> <br /> Realm: Freddy Fazbear's Pizza<br /> Actors: Freddy (all versions), Bonnie (all versions), Chica (all versions), Foxy (all versions), Balloon Boy, Marionette, Purple Guy<br /> Props: Cameras &amp; Screen, Electronic Doors, Freddy Mask, Systems, Flashlight<br /> Wisps: Phone Guy<br /> <br /> A True Fae that pits its slaves to work as &quot;security guards&quot; and constantly kills them again and again. So yeah, think about that next time you play FNAF.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't really like this idea, to be honest. I prefer to think of the bots as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-the-nwod?p=403482#post403482\"><b>Pandorans.</b></a> Besides, a True Fae with that many Titles would have Wyrd 19 and achieved Wyrd Transcendence multiple times. I'd say that this Gentry's only Titles are FF's Pizza (Realm), and all of the Bots as one Wisp. The rest is just the Realm's ephemera and strange laws dictated by the Wyrd, with the occasional and unfortunate changeling. The lack of a Title in Actor form increases the weirdness: how do people even end up there, if there is no leader sending Huntsmen and Loyalists to destabilize the Bulwarks of Courts? If anything, the Fazbear phenomenon could be an entire ghost franchise, with movies, toys, games and the like, but no traceable producers, manufacturers, or even a clear point of origin. A good Mystery for Mages to investigate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-18-2015, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T22:57:36-07:00","id":695741,"title":"","content":"I was reading through the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/168334-arkham-lost\"><b>Arkham Lost</b></a> seeting hack, and I wondered how exactly the Great Old Ones and Outer Gods would work as True Fae. The later lose some of their scope by being reduced to True Fae, but the former can still work.<br /> <br /> If I had to define the Outer Gods as a single Gentry, I'd say its Titles would be like this:<br /> <br /> Yog-Sothoth: The Key And The Gate. Most frequently takes the form of a Realm, with pulsating cosmic energies crystallizing into alien matter and fading back into quantum threads of time and fate. When in Realm form, its portals lead to and connect many places on Earth, as well as dimensions like the Astral, Underworld and Shadow. It can also become a Wisp consisting of floating spheres that are neither flesh nor light. This Title acts as a patron of sorts to sorcerers and scientists who seek the ultimate secrets of the universe.<br /> <br /> Azathoth: The Blind Idiot. In the Cthulhu Mythos, Azathoth is not conscious of all that it creates and destroys, and should it wake up, it is said all would cease to be. As a Title, it changes its manifestation with no apparent pattern. It usually appears as a gigantic Actor whose mere presence reshapes the Hedge around it for miles, making almost all of it pitch black and completely silent, save for the cacophonous piping and drumming. It is closer to a sleepwalker than mindless, occasionally lurching out of its throne and moving numbly through the Thorns, carrying the absolute dark and accursed music with it. Sometimes, its passing through the Thorns creates and destroys both trod and gate, sending hobgoblins out into the mortal world or trapping changelings inside the Hedge. It is said entire species of hobgoblins and Hedge towns are brought into existence and wiped out because of Azathoth.<br /> <br /> Nyarlathotep: The Crawling Chaos. The human disguise it takes in the eponymous story is the Actor manifestation, and it is the one which interacts with any Loyalists, Huntsmen and other servants. It is a master of Contracts that let it create wondrous devices, scare and awe people and assume monstrous forms. If need be, it can also become a Wisp to act in many places at once, with each instance an unique nightmare.<br /> <br /> The Necronomicon: The Forbidden Secrets Of Utmost Darkness. It is always manifested as a Prop in the form of a tome bound in human flesh and inked in blood. Many Tokens and other magic items have been made that mimic this Prop, but none hold as much power and pose as much danger. Within its pages one can learn all manner of Contracts accessible to anyone, but they all have costs that make them analogous to Goblin Contracts. Most involve the summoning of terrible hobgoblins or even Gentry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-18-2015, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T01:05:18-07:00","id":701830,"title":"","content":"Conqueror of the Universe, Frieza (Dragon Ball Z)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Lord Frieza. A tyrannical alien who invades and conquers inhabited planets either to auction them off or keep them for himself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Actor:</b>The Father (King Cold). Spoils Lord Frieza by giving him nearly anything he wants, but is mercilessly cruel with anybody else.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Actor:</b> The Son (Kuriza). Heir to Lord Frieza's empire, his head is vaguely shaped like a chestnut.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wisps:</b> The Soldiers (Various alien races enslaved by Frieza). Regarded as expendable, Lord Frieza does not hesitate to kill if they get in his line of fire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wisps:</b> The Ginyu Force. An immensely strong pack lead by the body snatching Captain Ginyu. They have a reputation for performing choreography before and during battle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Realm:</b> The Frieza Empire. A galaxy spanning empire with more than 100 planets conquered by Frieza alone!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Prop:</b> The Mothership. A circular shaped craft which Frieza travels the cosmos in. It is capable of carrying over a thousand Soldiers inside!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-23-2015, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T19:41:42-07:00","id":706104,"title":"","content":"Ruin, from Brandon Sanderson's Mistborn<br /> <br /> Actor: The Lord Ruler<br /> <br /> Realm: The World of Ash<br /> <br /> Wisps: The Steel Inquisitors<br /> <br /> Prop: Atium","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T07:30:01-07:00","id":706812,"title":"","content":"Don\u00b4t forget the Gentry doesn\u00b4t need to play so many Actors, that\u00b4s what goblins companions and recruited loyal changelings are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T08:42:14-07:00","id":706971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327064-let-s-make-antagonists-of-fantasy-series-into-true-fae?p=706812#post706812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u00b4t forget the Gentry doesn\u00b4t need to play so many Actors, that\u00b4s what goblins companions and recruited loyal changelings are for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also not every object is a Prop and not every place is a Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T09:27:33-07:00","id":706993,"title":"","content":"For example, in a Fazbear 's Pizza scenario the animatronics would be former children now extremely mutated changelings without any trace of sanity. The only actors would be the Marionette<br /> and/or the Purple Guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T09:27:37-07:00","id":706994,"title":"","content":"Yeah, some of these True Fae would have Transcended if they had as many titles as suggested.<br /> <br /> Hobgoblins and Changelings can and will make up some of the cast, guys. :/<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, keep in mind a distinction between Realms and Domains. Some Realms are vast, others are small, but Realms are always implied to be active settings, seemingly possessing a will and desire or at least acts as a significant extension of the Fae's will, while Domains are passive. Jareth's Labyrinth is a Realm, Sauron's Mordor is a Domain. Referencing Getbackers (Though no one's read it), Infinity Fortress is a Realm, Shinjuku is a Domain.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Dungeons in Zelda games are likely Realms while the overworlds are Domains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-18-2015, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T11:42:35-07:00","id":707174,"title":"","content":"Okay so I admit I wasn't considering Transcendance. It was originally a thought exercise limited to the True Fae and their manifestations alone. &lt;,&lt;<br /> <br /> Domains as well as Hobgoblin and Changeling subordinates are pertinent factors in describing the Gentry as antagonists though, that is very much true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T14:16:52-07:00","id":707381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327064-let-s-make-antagonists-of-fantasy-series-into-true-fae?p=707174#post707174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so I admit I wasn't considering Transcendance. It was originally a thought exercise limited to the True Fae and their manifestations alone. &lt;,&lt;<br /> <br /> Domains as well as Hobgoblin and Changeling subordinates are pertinent factors in describing the Gentry as antagonists though, that is very much true.</div> </div> </div> </div>When people have hit the point of not describing the Ginyu Force as a Wisp I feel the purpose of manifestation bears emphasis. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T07:20:37-07:00","id":718927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327064-let-s-make-antagonists-of-fantasy-series-into-true-fae?p=707381#post707381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When people have hit the point of not describing the Ginyu Force as a Wisp I feel the purpose of manifestation bears emphasis. :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Meh, I went back and removed the Ginyu's, Zarbon and Vegeta as Actors, because I don't think a Fae would take a roll that opposes itself, while Ginyu and Zarbon could just be powerful loyalists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T08:42:11-07:00","id":719389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327064-let-s-make-antagonists-of-fantasy-series-into-true-fae?p=706993#post706993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, in a Fazbear 's Pizza scenario the animatronics would be former children now extremely mutated changelings without any trace of sanity. The only actors would be the Marionette<br /> and/or the Purple Guy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But the purple guy became Springtrap. Hmmm, actually, would he be considered a Huntsman? He is the one responsible for luring the kids away and killing them, thus allowing the puppet to stuff them in suits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T06:39:55-07:00","id":722787,"title":"","content":"<b>Name:</b> Darkness and Light<br /> <br /> <b>Domain:</b> Final Fantasy<br /> <br /> <b>Actor:</b> Final Boss. Monolythic in size and godlike in power, it's body is an almagamation of religious symbolism. This Actor only appears when Darkness or Light begins to overwhelm the other and is believed to be the avatar of the stronger Fae.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Actor:</b> The Four Crystals. Governing the elements of Fire, Water, Wind and Earth, the crystals maintain balance and order within the realm. In times of great crisis when Darkness or Light become too powerful, the crystals select four warriors to journey forth and restore the peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wisp:</b> Judges. The local law enforcement, they are tasked with keeping the citizens of Ivalice under control.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Realm:</b> Ivalice. A vast country home to a multitude of different races. Its culture is unique for combining medieval fantasy and science fiction in the same era.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Prop:</b> Magicite. The magic of Arcadia transformed into a crystaline substance, Magicite can be used as an alternative power source for machinery, granting them a nearly infinite supply of clean running energy!<br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> The domain of Final Fantasy is home to two Gentry who share it with each other, though not by their own choice. Darkness and Light are in a never ending war for dominance, one side representing evil and the other representing good. As long as they remain in a stalemate, the domain has some resemblance of order to it. But should either side become powerful enough to win the war, they inadvertently begin to destroy the domain they built together. In order to avoid the death of their realm and continue their mutual survival, they created the Four Crystals to serve as arbiters in the war. If they detect one side is beginning to overpower the other, they select four warriors to aid the weakened Gentry in restoring the balance.<br /> <br /> It is unclear whether these warriors are another manifestation of the Fae or if they are Changelings blessed with enormous power, but by working together, they venture through the realm, defeating scores of monsters and finally confronting the avatar of Light or Darkness, defeating them in battle and bringing peace to the realm. Once both sides have recovered from their losses, the war is back on!<br /> <br /> The Hedge which surrounds and secures Final Fantasy takes the shape of a thick mist that emanates from tunnels and fissures beneath the ground. Those who venture inside the mist draw the attention of monstrous Hedge creatures that attack on sight. Thus, most inhabitants of Ivalice avoid the mist, unless they're attempting to escape, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-24-2015, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T04:51:21-07:00","id":731928,"title":"","content":"Here's one that'll make someone I know happy;<br /> <br /> <b>King Haggard </b>from <b><i>The Last Unicorn</i></b><br /> Realm: The Dreary Kingdom of Hagsgate<br /> Realm: The Ocean of Seafoam Unicorns<br /> Actor: The Red Bull<br /> Actor: Mabruk the Court Magician<br /> Actor:<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Prince L\u00edr</span></span></span><br /> Props: The Clock, Gateway to the Red Bull's Lair<br /> Wisps: The Thirsty Dead<br /> <br /> In retrospect though, Prince Lir would probably actually be a changeling rather than an Actor - the adopted son who is distinguished from his father by being capable of love? Sounds like a Fairest changeling to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8485,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","user":"Random_Interrupt","date":". 10-27-2015, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T14:31:49-08:00","id":750114,"title":"","content":"The Hellraiser Cenobites (from the first film, the second, and the comic series) work very well<br /> <br /> True Fae: Leviathan<br /> Actors 1-4: Pinhead, the Female, Chatterer, and Butterball<br /> Prop: the Lament Configuration<br /> Realm: The Monastery of the Cenobites<br /> <br /> <br /> Spoilers below this point<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Each of the Actors is a title wrapped around a former Changeling that never actually escaped from the clutches of Leviathan; each one has forgotten their origin, and surrendered to the title that they act as the base for. They also wield emotional powers similar to or based on the Courts of Spring (Desire), Fall (Fear), the South (Ecstasy) and the North (Suffering), which are the emotions they tend to feed on. Each also has the Mantle benefits of the North Mantle, though their Meins take on unique alterations rather than the usual ones of the North Court.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T16:18:29-08:00","id":750250,"title":"","content":"<b>Here's some Ideas.</b><br /> <br /> Steven Universe<br /> <br /> Peter Pan<br /> <br /> Megaman (any iteration)<br /> <br /> Transformers (any iteration)<br /> <br /> Happy Tree Friends","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T16:37:32-08:00","id":750266,"title":"","content":"<b>True Fae:</b> Mon-Do Med-ia<br /> <b>Realm:</b> The Forest of Infinite Deaths<br /> <b>Realm:</b> The City of Wonton Disaster<br /> <b>Actor:</b> The Blue Idiot<br /> <b>Actor:</b> The Torn Soldier<br /> <b>Wisps:</b> Unfortunate Accidents<br /> <b>Prop:</b> The Idol. Traveling through the realm of its own accord, this statuette brings fatal luck to any who possess it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-02-2015, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T17:00:53-08:00","id":750292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slimjimjohnson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327064-let-s-make-antagonists-of-fantasy-series-into-true-fae?p=631023#post631023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YHWH, God the creator<br /> Actor- The son (Jesus)<br /> Actor- The deceiver (Lucifer)<br /> Realm- Heaven<br /> Realm- Hell<br /> Wisps- The choir of angels<br /> Wisps- The fallen<br /> Prop- Holy grail (cup of life)<br /> <br /> Pretending to his captives that he is at war with another powerful being (satan) he uses the idea of free will in his realms to create legends off of changeling warfare that believe they are fighting for one side or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>This certainly explains why God was unable to overcome the people of the plains, who had chariots of iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T10:51:46-08:00","id":756928,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Name: The Yawning Void of Madness<br /> Actor: The Childlike Emperess<br /> Actor: Xayide<br /> Realm: Fantasia<br /> Wisps: Atreyu, Gmork, Falcore<br /> Prop: </span></span>AURYN<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Uses stories of grand adventures to trick people into accepting fantasy, delusion and madness and reject reality when faced with the fear of weakness, oblivion and a meaningless of existence. </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T11:31:51-08:00","id":760108,"title":"","content":"<b>Name:</b> The Living Machine<br /> <br /> <b>Actor:</b> The Blue Bomber (Mega Man)<br /> <br /> <b>Actor:</b> The Giver of Life (Dr. Light)<br /> <br /> <b>Actor:</b> The Giver of Hope (Dr. Wily)<br /> <br /> <b>Actor:</b> The Blues Brother (Proto Man)<br /> <br /> <b>Wisps:</b> The Pre-Programmed (Mechaniloids)<br /> <br /> <b>Realm:</b> Mega City<br /> <br /> <b>Realm:</b> Doctor Wily's Fortress<br /> <br /> <b>Prop:</b> Rush. Mega Man's robotic canine, it is capable of shifting into three different modes of transportation.<br /> <br /> <b>Prop:</b> Proto Shield. A nearly indestructible shield used by Proto Man to deflect energy weapons.<br /> <br /> <b>Prop:</b> The Wily Capsule. Dr. Wily's flying escape pod, known for its high pitched whine when piloted.<br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Details:</b> The Living Machine is a Fae who's realm is a futuristic world where most of the working class is populated by robots. For decades, robots were incapable of doing anything outside of their programming, until the brilliant Doctor Light successfully created a robot that was capable of thinking for itself, exhibiting behavior that almost perfectly mimicked humans. That's probably because they used to be humans, stolen away from earth to become part of The Living Machine's realm!<br /> <br /> At first, these new robots toiled away happily in the city until they learned a shocking truth. They had an expiration date and would eventually break down over time. Faced with their own mortality, the robots began to act out, losing their desire to work. The Living Machine needed some way to restore them to proper service, so a new doctor was revealed. Although he lacked the knowledge of how to create sentient life, the new Doctor Wily was able to upgrade and repair damaged machinery. He approached the rebellious robots with an offer; if they agreed to serve him, he would ensure they survived past their expiration date. Many agreed to the terms and soon Dr. Wily had a whole army of robots at his beck and call.<br /> <br /> But the Fae rarely offer compassion so freely and this one was no different. Dr. Wily had grown jealous of Doctor Light's brilliant talent with machines. Once he had an army of his own, he declared war upon his rival, desperate to prove himself the greater scientist. Perhaps he might have won, had it not been for Light's greatest masterpiece, a robot he named Mega Man. A modified fighting machine, Mega Man was worth over a hundred soldiers and fought his way through Dr. Wily's army of robots countless times. Defeating the mad doctor in battle, only for him to escape and try again later. Doctor Wily even succeeded in recruiting Proto Man, the first robot created by Doctor Light and a precursor to Mega Man, but ultimately failed to achieve victory over The Blue Bomber time and again.<br /> <br /> But now things are beginning to change, some of the robots who joined Dr. Wily are beginning to see the pattern for what it is and have decided they will no longer be part of it. This time when Dr. Wily offered them longevity, they turned it down, choosing instead make the best of the time they had left, rather than attempt to prolong the inevitable. They chose to abandon Mega City, a decision that The Living Machine found intolerable. Once again, the robots were starting to abandon their role as servitors in favor of their own selfish desires, they needed to be shown the error of their ways. They needed to be reprogrammed into dutiful servants, their memory purged of these selfish personalities. That's when it decided to unleash its huntsmen to track them down again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T12:28:35-08:00","id":760143,"title":"","content":"\u2026A brief reminder to everyone making singular Fae as entire continuities:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Equinox Road, p83</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A faerie\u2019s name is the heart of its being. Gentry have many kinds of names, from a simple \u201cAyesha\u201d or \u201cJohn\u201d to the sound of waves breaking against an ice shelf, or a picture of the <i>wadjet</i>: the Egyptian symbol of magic.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Titles are abstract (and even enigmatic) concepts but they always refer to an emotion, sensual experience or object.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Equinox Road, p83-4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of air, water, food or shelter, the Gentry need to struggle. They need adversity, surprise and risk. They can\u2019t create these conditions by themselves. Fae can simulate all of these things, but it\u2019s a meaningless exercise. [\u2026] None of it sustains the faerie. At best, it\u2019s a diversion, like daydreaming or masturbation. At worst it's autocannibalism; the desperate faerie mimics a true conflict to deny her own starvation. In fact, the most spectacular vistas in all Arcadia are often created this way, by desperate Gentry on the verge of fading away. [\u2026] This fate may not be death, but Gentry fear it. They cerate Feuds to stave it off: covenants of Gentry who vow to plot against each other. Each faerie in a Feud sends manifestations of itself against others, where they play out tales of genuine peril and difficult victory.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-07-2015, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T21:48:55-08:00","id":760495,"title":"","content":"My spin on Utena.<br /> <br /> <b>True Fae: </b>The Ends Of The World<br /> <br /> <b>Name Actor: </b>The Quixotic King of Lustful Dominance (Akio Ohtori)<br /> <br /> <b>Realm: </b>The Coffin of Misguided Desires (Ohtori Academy)<br /> <br /> <b>Prop: </b>The Blade of The Betrayed Martyr (The Sword of Dios)<br /> <br /> <b>Wisps: </b>The Selfish Edges (The Swords of Hate)<br /> <br /> <b>Actor: </b>The Prisoner's Despairing Trophy (The Rose Bride)<br /> <br /> Naturally, that last one became one of the few Banished to gleefully accept that fate, and Clarity with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 11-08-2015, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T11:02:17-08:00","id":760765,"title":"","content":"How powerful would a Fae have to be to have seven actors? I'm kinda imagining YISUN from Kill Six Billion Demons as an uber-powerful Fae with the seven demiurges as its Actors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T11:49:48-08:00","id":760807,"title":"","content":"YISUN is... more like the Wyrd with the multiplicity of gods as the Gentry, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T16:57:53-08:00","id":829466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327064-let-s-make-antagonists-of-fantasy-series-into-true-fae?p=706994#post706994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, some of these True Fae would have Transcended if they had as many titles as suggested.<br /> <br /> Hobgoblins and Changelings can and will make up some of the cast, guys. :/<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, keep in mind a distinction between Realms and Domains. Some Realms are vast, others are small, but Realms are always implied to be active settings, seemingly possessing a will and desire or at least acts as a significant extension of the Fae's will, while Domains are passive. Jareth's Labyrinth is a Realm, Sauron's Mordor is a Domain. Referencing Getbackers (Though no one's read it), Infinity Fortress is a Realm, Shinjuku is a Domain.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Dungeons in Zelda games are likely Realms while the overworlds are Domains.</div> </div> </div> </div> What do you think it happens when they Transcend? i know theres no canon definitive answer ut i always like to hear people opinions on that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T18:47:54-08:00","id":829501,"title":"","content":"They write up a character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T19:00:28-08:00","id":829512,"title":"","content":"My attempt at giving epithets to the Slender Man.<br /> <br /> <b>True Name: </b>The Looming Shadow-Idea<br /> <br /> <b>Titles:</b> The Apparition Of Towering Dread (Actor), The Nebulous Encroaching Of Isolation (Realm), The Invitation Of Playfulness From Around The Corner (Wisp)<br /> <br /> I tried to make the True Name sound like an antiquated way of referring to a meme or thought-form. The Titles were as vague as possible to have just enough menace between each word, and to keep the visuals of their manifestation versatile. For example, the Realm can be a frigid underground maze just as easily as a twilit forest clouded in fog, which Wraith_Magus narrated beautifully in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/416820-if-the-slender-man-was-a-true-fae-what-would-his-realm-be-like?p=416928#post416928\"><b>this post.</b></a><br /> <br /> The Wisp is a personal addition of mine. I see Slendy as something akin to a ghostly, needy father figure. Its mind is not quite as alien as some speculate. It understands that mortals are more willing to approach things they are familiar with, and its favored type of mortal are children. As a logical conclusion, its Wisp consists of mirage-children and phantom-pets that are meant to lure and entrap. They are more communicative than their &quot;daddy&quot;, and tend to stick around for a bit longer, but they suffer from the same kind of tells. Behind their Masks, they are patchwork creatures made of whatever they can take from those they spirit away, especially toys, pictures and other items of emotional value.<br /> <br /> The Proxies are not a Wisp. They are a collective of Loyalists, be they humans, changelings or hobgoblins. The occasional Huntsman may be supported by Proxies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T20:27:46-08:00","id":829538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/327064-let-s-make-antagonists-of-fantasy-series-into-true-fae?p=829501#post829501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They write up a character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>They become people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0